# Version control

Full SOP: [docs/sop/version-control.md](docs/sop/version-control.md).
Version file: [VERSION.md](VERSION.md).
Working ledger: [WORKING.md](WORKING.md) · [working-files skill](.cursor/skills/working-files/SKILL.md).
PR closing: [github-prs skill](.cursor/skills/github-prs/SKILL.md).

## Semver

- **MAJOR** — breaking contracts / rewrite
- **MINOR** — backward-compatible features (`release/vX.Y.0`)
- **PATCH** — bugs/docs/polish (`release/vX.Y.Z`)
- Keep **all three** in sync on every bump: `VERSION.md`, root `package.json`, README **Version:**
- Bump `services/api` version only when API behavior/contract changes
- One release line at a time — if new work needs the **next** version and Ready-to-ship exists, recommend PR first (working-files / github-prs skills)

## Branches & labels

- Work on `release/vX.Y.Z` matching the version being shipped
- Label issues/PRs with `vX.Y.Z`
- Merge to `main` via PR only; no force-push to shared branches

## Cross-session work

- Keep [WORKING.md](WORKING.md) updated when finishing issues so the next chat can batch a release PR
- Ready-to-ship issues become the PR **Closes** list (see github-prs skill)
- Do not start next-version features on the current line while Ready-to-ship is unshipped — ship first

## Issues & PRs

- Close finished issues **only** with PR body `Closes #N` (never `gh issue close` for PR work)
- Release PRs: Summary, Test plan, and a complete **Closes** section
- Do **not** open a PR until QA + `VERSION.md` sync + **explicit human approval** (implementation done ≠ open PR)
